From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Contrast detection autofocus for VCM lenses

The simple pipeline ignores a sensor's focus lens, so cameras like the
Surface Pro 7 rear (ov8865 + dw9719) sit at a fixed focus.

- SwStatsCpu gathers a focus measure: green contrast between neighbouring
  sampled cells in the centre third, plus the green level to normalise it.
- The soft IPA gets the lens range at init and can emit a lens position,
  which the simple pipeline applies through CameraLens.
- New Af algorithm: once exposure has settled, sweep the lens from far to
  near one step per statistics frame (crediting each measurement to the
  move in effect for its frame), stop past the peak, refine it with a
  Gaussian fit, and sweep again when the scene changes and settles.
  Enabled from the tuning file; ov8865.yaml turns it on.

